course: dictionary
lesson: 12898
title: Being equipped
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Equipped means having the tools, machines or things you need for a job or activity. «The science lab was well equipped with microscopes and test tubes.» Well-equipped means the lab had everything the scientists needed.
explain: Equipped can also mean having the skills or knowledge you need. «Mia was equipped to climb the mountain, because she had practised all summer.» Mia was ready because she had the skills, not because she had a tool.
explain: Look for the small words after equipped. Equipped with is followed by things you have, and equipped for is followed by the job or activity. «The explorers were equipped with ropes and torches.» The word with tells you what they carried.
fact: Equipped is the past form of the verb equip.
fact: «Well-equipped» means having many good tools or things you need.
fact: «Equipped with» is followed by the things you have, such as «equipped with ropes and torches».
fact: «Equipped for» is followed by the job or activity, such as «equipped for the cold».
fact: In school, being equipped for lessons means having your pencil, ruler and so on.
exercise: «The explorers were equipped with ropes and torches.» What does equipped mean here? | Were lost in the forest | * Had the things they needed | Were very tired | Were going home
exercise: Ben says «My lab is well-equipped» means his lab is messy. What does well-equipped mean? | Closed for the day | Very messy and dirty | * Having the tools and machines a job needs | Very small
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Mia was equipped for the race.» that is the past form of equip. | was | race | * equipped | Mia
test: «Our class was equipped for science with goggles and beakers.» What does equipped mean? | Lost in a lab | Sad and tired | * Had everything needed for the job | Very quiet
test: «Ruby was equipped to lead the team, because she knew all the rules.» What does equipped to mean? | Had a lot of tools | * Had the skills or knowledge needed | Had no idea | Had gone home
exam: «The hikers were well equipped with warm coats, maps and water.» What does this tell us about the hikers? | They were tired of walking | They had left their maps at home | * They had everything they needed | They were lost and cold
